                <pb facs="0434" n="425" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg425"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/246: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-13T16:00:00-04:00">January 13, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. Reference my No. 12, January 12, 6 p.m. Have now elicited from Garcia<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d433-f1"/> oral declaration that in so far as they lie within
                    the administrative authority of the Chilean Government the provisions on other
                    than customs matters in the <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi>, such as
                    exchange, will be given practical effect at once and continuously pending
                    approval by Congress. This statement will be included in a note addressed to the
                    Embassy by the Foreign Minister in reply to a note to be addressed to him by me
                    making inquiry as to the legal steps respecting the entry into effect of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi>, if the Department approves this
                    exchange of notes. The <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> is thus in
                    provisional effect already from a practical standpoint; but is not in
                    provisional effect from the technical standpoint explained in my previous
                    telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d433-f1" n="11" xml:id="d433-f1-content">
                <p>Desiderio García, Under Secretary of Commerce, Ministry for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
